{"chunk_id": "b84d7833f452", "text": "Sita, imprisoned in Lanka, falls into deep despair, believing Rama may be dead or unaware of her survival. Surrounded by threatening demonesses, she contemplates death rather than life without him. At this moment the aged rakshasi Trijata intervenes, recounting a prophetic dream that terrifies the others. In her vision, Rama and Lakshmana appear in dazzling celestial splendor, traveling through the sky and ultimately reunited with Sita, who shines beside Rama like light beside the sun. The dream then shifts to ominous symbols: Ravana humiliated, drunken, dragged toward death, while Lanka burns and sinks into ruin. Vibhishana alone appears honored beneath a white canopy. Trijata interprets the dream as a clear omen\u2014the destruction of the rakshasas and the imminent victory of Rama\u2014warning the demonesses that tormenting Sita will bring their annihilation.\nThe rakshasi Trijata recounts a prophetic dream foretelling Rama\u2019s victory, Sita\u2019s reunion with him, and the downfall of Ravana and Lanka.\nThemes: prophetic dream, doom of Ravana, hope for Sita, divine justice, omens", "vector": [-0.005550323519855738, -0.026882290840148926, 0.010291503742337227, -0.0003458503633737564, -0.006543363444507122, 0.01259187888354063, -0.033836912363767624, -0.018229136243462563, -0.019339200109243393, -0.014417467638850212, 0.010050767101347446, 0.02165294997394085, 0.007489593233913183, 0.0009336915099993348, -0.004460320342332125, 0.003637802554294467, 0.042235955595970154, -0.018817603588104248, 0.0352545864880085, -0.021893685683608055, 0.002002797555178404, -0.018082018941640854, 0.000743943965062499, 0.016704468056559563, -0.023418353870511055, 0.0026564651634544134, 0.020569633692502975, -0.04017631709575653, 0.02052951045334339, -0.008793585002422333, -0.010003956966102123, -0.013501329347491264, -0.010351687669754028, -0.004212896339595318, -0.019887546077370644, 0.0071752979420125484, 0.005426611751317978, -0.0105589888